.TH BINGUX-FILES 1 "2026-10-28" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-files \- file manager for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-files
.RI [ FOLDER | FILE | URI ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-files
opens the Files window with tabs, a places sidebar, list and grid views,
previews and file operations.
With no argument it opens the home folder, or raises the window when it is
already open.
.PP
Only one Files window runs.
A second launch hands its folder to the running window, which opens it in a new
tab and comes to the front.
Only the first argument is used.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FOLDER
A folder path.
.B ~
and relative paths are accepted; a relative path is relative to the current
directory.
.TP
.I FILE
A file path. Files opens the folder that holds it.
.TP
.I URI
.BR file:///path ,
.B recent:///
for the recent files, or
.BR bingux\-files://path .
.SH DEFAULT FILE MANAGER
The desktop entry lists
.BR inode/directory .
To open folders in Files, run:
.PP
.RS
.B xdg\-mime default bingux\-files.desktop inode/directory
.RE
.PP
or choose it under Settings, Applications, Default applications.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/bingux/files/view.json
Each folder's icon size and sort order, and the window size.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bingux/files/v1/
Cached folder listings.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash/
Where deleted files go (the freedesktop.org Trash).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/recently-used.xbel
The recent files list.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1),
.BR xdg\-mime (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/files.md in the Bingux source.
